@startuml
title Role assignment per data direction

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "gatewayd (ASIL-B)" {
  component "application facing\nmw::com" as gw_app
  component "Gateway IPC Binding\n(mw::com implementation)" as gw_bind
}

package "someipd (QM)" {
  component "Gateway IPC Binding\n(mw::com implementation)" as sd_bind
  component "vsomeip\nnetwork" as sd_net
}

note top of gw_bind
  provider role for local service instances
  consumer role for remote service instances
end note

note top of sd_bind
  consumer role for local service instances
  provider role for remote service instances
end note

gw_app -down-> gw_bind : SOCom Server_connector\n(local service instance)
gw_bind -right-> sd_bind : GenericSkeleton -> GenericProxy\napplication to network
sd_bind -down-> sd_net : SOCom Client_connector

sd_net -up-> sd_bind : SOCom Server_connector\n(remote service instance)
sd_bind -left-> gw_bind : GenericSkeleton -> GenericProxy\nnetwork to application
gw_bind -up-> gw_app : SOCom Client_connector

note bottom
  The peer that owns the data source owns the GenericSkeleton.
  The peer that consumes owns the GenericProxy.
  Roles are fixed at startup, see decision D4.
end note
@enduml
